{"n":16,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.00","body":"address: 0401\ntitle: first-build\nstate: draft\ntype: workflow\naxioms: 1.5.9\nband: dev\nthousands: 0"}
{"n":17,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.01","body":"## frame\ntype: rule\naxioms: 5.1\n\nShow the plan. Stop before code. The person approves a revision of this page, or no pack is written.\n\n## first-build\ntype: rule\naxioms: 5.2\n\nRust core only. Parse, replay, torn line, writer API, fixture 10.11.21 page 1001.timer with a face 04 why.\n\n## checks\ntype: rule\naxioms: 5.9\n\nFive checks, unnamed as a pack until this page is approved. Evidence is the fixture file and the test output, not a summary.\n\n## left-out\ntype: rule\naxioms: 5.7\n\nCompute process, app, transport, snapshots, forks, drafting ops, brands, kernel fill, task failure, hardware.\n\n## sources\ntype: rule\naxioms: 2.6\n\nInherit Axioms, settled decisions, decided format, seqAddr, brands, drafting, Design. workflow-loop.md is draft placement, not live law. kernel-design.md is proposed.\n\n## clash\ntype: rule\naxioms: 7.8\n\nA2.6 example says 05 is build. workflow-loop.md says 03 is build and 05 is jobs. This book uses the second for placement only."}
{"n":18,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.02","body":"## checks\ntype: schema\naxioms: 5.9\n\nDone only when all five hold, and not before the person approves this page:\n\n1. A full address parses. A short address expands against one active book. A bad width is rejected, not padded. A leading dot resolves against one active page and is refused when more than one page is active.\n2. A .book file replays to current faces. A put creates. A tail moves only from the current tail. A partial last line is dropped and earlier entries still replay.\n3. The writer API is the only way to append.\n4. Fixture book 10.11.21: identity 0000, page 1001 title timer, faces 00, 01, and 04, card purpose, with why: on face 04.\n5. A person can open that fixture in an editor and read the why."}
{"n":19,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.04","body":"## frame\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / frame]\naxioms: 5.1.4\nwhy: The ask was to see the plan before any build is authorized. Without that edge, the next step becomes code.\n\nThis page is the dev page for one subject, first-build, in the 0-thousands. The person asked for the Workshop root to be read, notes taken, and a temp book stood here. Subdirectories were not taken as sources.\n\nWhat done looks like for this pass: the person can read this book and say whether the frame is right. What done does not look like: a repository, a crate, or a pack on 0501.\n\nApproval, when it comes, is of one revision of this page. A later edit of the page is not that approval.\n\n## first-build\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / first-build]\naxioms: 5.2.4\nwhy: format.md already chose the file and the language, and agents.003.md already named the first slice. The page records that slice so a later pack has something exact to point at.\n\nThe core is a Rust library: address parser and validator, book reader and writer, tail rules. The compute is a later program. The Next.js reader is later still, and it is meant to use this core as WebAssembly so the two cannot disagree about an address.\n\nThe fixture book 10.11.21 is the proof inside that slice. It is not this temp book. This book is the plan. The fixture is not created until a pack on 0501 is approved and claimed.\n\nCode, when it exists, stays in the repo. This book keeps the why. Face 08 on 0301 will link the repo paths, with the commit they were checked at. Those links do not exist yet.\n\n## checks\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / checks], [02 / checks]\naxioms: 5.9.4\nwhy: A builder's report of done is not proof. The five checks are the acceptance criteria a reviewer can open.\n\nEach check is a behavior of the core, not a module layout. A partial last line must drop without damaging earlier entries, because intelligence bleeds and a bad stop must leave a book a person can still read. The why on the fixture's face 04 is how a person checks the slice without a program written to explain it.\n\nThese checks are proposed criteria. They are not a grant.\n\n## left-out\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / left-out]\naxioms: 5.7.4\nwhy: The open list is the edge of the frame. Solving it inside the first slice would hide unfinished decisions inside code.\n\nLeft out on purpose: the compute process and its queue; how clients talk to it; the Next.js app; snapshots and archives; fork reconciliation; proposal batches; drafting operations copy, note, merge, and promote; dictionary meters and new brand placement; filling kernel pages; a rejected review; a worker that dies while open; hardware.\n\nworkflow-loop.md section 10 still has open mechanism questions: the risk rubric, claim recovery, what counts as a material edit of an approved page, the promotion record, continuation allocation, evidence by work type, and a write that touches two book files. None of those are decided here.\n\n## sources\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / sources]\naxioms: 2.6.4\nwhy: A second shape, or a second reading of a settled choice, has to say which source it refused. This page inherits.\n\nRead, in order, from the Workshop root: AGENTS.md, then Axioms.md, agents.003.md, brands.md, decisions.md, Design.md, drafting.md, format.md, kernel-design.md, review.md, seqAddr.md, workflow-loop.md. Folders under the root were not reviewed.\n\nSettled addresses, faces, the book log, and the Rust split are not reopened. kernel-design.md is a proposal. review.md is an older condensation, not a second law. workflow-loop.md says it is a draft and not live. It is used here for where a page sits, because that is what was asked, and for no other grant.\n\n## clash\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / clash]\naxioms: 7.4.8\nwhy: Two written band maps disagree. Picking one in silence would make the other look settled.\n\nDecision A2.6 and seqAddr.md section 6.1 give the example 0423 as dev and 0523 as build. workflow-loop.md, still marked draft, specializes the bands as 03 build, 04 dev, 05 jobs, and 07 colab, and says the older example is not authority to overwrite that specialization. It also says not to edit seqAddr on the quiet.\n\nThis book places the work on the workflow-loop map, in the 0-thousands: doors 0300, 0400, 0500, and 0700, subject 01 titled first-build. seqAddr.md and decisions.md were not changed. The clash remains missing authority, recorded as question 0401.05.02."}
{"n":20,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.08","body":"## first-build\ntype: link\naxioms: 8.7\nkind: 7\nwhy: Face 08 link kinds are not settled (C4). These lines are for a person to read. They are not a compute link, and a matching title is not the connection.\n\nSet, same subject 01 in the 0-thousands:\n\n- 0301.first-build — build. Stood empty. Back-link 0301.08.\n- 0401.first-build — dev. This page.\n- 0501.first-build — jobs. No pack. Back-link 0501.08.\n- 0701.first-build — colab. No trial. Back-link 0701.08.\n\nNot a continuation. Overflow, if it ever happens, waits for a PP99 pointer. None is written.\n\nRoot files this page inherited: AGENTS.md, Axioms.md, agents.003.md, brands.md, decisions.md, Design.md, drafting.md, format.md, kernel-design.md, review.md, seqAddr.md, workflow-loop.md."}
{"n":21,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.05.01","body":"## assign-address\ntype: task\naxioms: 7.1\ntitle: The book header is 7.\nstate: question\n\nDesk, shelf, and book were not granted. Inventing a number would claim a desk. What address should this workbook carry before any later pack is allowed to name it?","tail":"draft"}
{"n":22,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.05.02","body":"## band-map\ntype: task\naxioms: 7.1\ntitle: Two maps are in the root.\nstate: question\n\nA2.6's example calls band 05 build. workflow-loop.md calls band 03 build and band 05 jobs, and it is still a draft. This book followed the draft for placement because the 0-thousands were requested. Is that placement accepted for this book only, and will A2.6 be updated on its own drafting path?","tail":"draft"}
{"n":23,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.05.03","body":"## loop-not-live\ntype: task\naxioms: 7.1\ntitle: workflow-loop.md is not live.\nstate: question\n\nIts own header says Director review is required and the text is not live. This book uses its band doors and its rule that code stays in the repo. Which of those may be used before the loop document itself is approved?","tail":"draft"}
{"n":24,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.05.04","body":"## confirm-scope\ntype: task\naxioms: 7.1\ntitle: The first slice is the core.\nstate: question\n\nagents.003.md limits the first build to the Rust core and five checks. Confirm that scope, or mark what must be added, before any pack is written on 0501.","tail":"draft"}
{"n":25,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0401.06.01","body":"## root-read\ntype: note\naxioms: 6.4\nby: cursor\nrefs: 0401.04, 0401.05.01, 0401.05.02\nwhy: The read has to be recoverable without this chat.\n\nRead the Workshop root, and not its subdirectories: AGENTS.md first, then agents.003.md, Axioms.md, brands.md, decisions.md, Design.md, drafting.md, format.md, kernel-design.md, review.md, seqAddr.md, and workflow-loop.md.\n\nAGENTS.md now names compute, the database, and a Next.js UI. It no longer says design only. agents.003.md says building has not started. This request asks for the plan to be visible first, so the book is stood and no code is written.\n\nThe book file is append-only JSON Lines, one book per container, Rust core, Rust compute, TypeScript app. Those choices stay as format.md decided them. SQLite remains the fallback if the log is too slow. ZIP, a folder of face files, a file edited in place, and a CRDT were set aside there.\n\nAxioms are the shape and seqAddr is the geometry. Cite with axioms:. A cite permits nothing. Cold check before a write is 1.7.8. This file was written with no compute to enforce that check. The gap is on 0000.04.\n\nNotes metadata is still open (C7). The fields on this note are a reading aid, not a settled schema.\n\nA filename search for the words 0 thousands matched root workflow-loop.md and also paths under director/ and claude/. Those folders were not reviewed and are not sources for this page.\n\nUnresolved on purpose: the four questions on 0401.05, plus the open list on card left-out. Nothing in this note settles them.","tail":"draft"}
{"n":26,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0301.00","body":"address: 0301\ntitle: first-build\nstate: draft\ntype: workflow\naxioms: 8.5\nband: build\nthousands: 0"}
{"n":27,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0301.01","body":"## held\ntype: rule\naxioms: 5.1\n\nSubject first-build, role build. Stood so the dev page has a set. No work is granted."}
{"n":28,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0301.04","body":"## held\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / held]\naxioms: 5.1.4.8\nwhy: A dev page that names a build, a job, or a trial with nothing at that address is a missing connection. Standing the page is not permission to fill it.\n\nNo module is described here yet. When a build is authorized, face 01 will say what the module is, face 02 will name its files, and face 08 will link those repo paths with the commit last checked. Code will not be pasted into this book."}
{"n":29,"at":"2026-11-11T19:02:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"0301.08","body":"## first-build\ntype: link\naxioms: 8.7\nkind: 7\nwhy: The set is written both ways so a person can walk it. Link kinds are not settled.\n\nThis page is 0301.first-build, role build.\nDev page: 0401.first-build.\nAlso in the set: 0301 build, 0501 jobs, 0701 colab.\nBack to this page from 0401.08."}
