{"n":68,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0504.05.01","body":"by: cursor\nauthorized: person-2026-11-11-next-pages\nlead: M\naxioms: 5.2\noutcome: seqbook check fails a page of only face 07, and fails a page with no face 00.\noverview: The page-shape rule from C1 runs against a book file.\nstop if: The work needs the compute, or a change to which faces count.\ngrant: core/src/check.rs, core/src/bin/seqbook.rs, core/tests/next_pages.rs, and appends to cursor/temp.book.\nframe: page-shape\nrisk: 2\npredecessor: 10.10.10.0403\n\n## w01\ntype: work\ntitle: Check the page shape\naxioms: 5.2\nreason: Face 00 and a content face are what make an address a page rather than a loose note.\npath: core/src/check.rs\n","tail":"draft"}
{"n":69,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0302.00","body":"address: 0302\ntitle: read\nstate: draft\ntype: workflow\naxioms: 8.6\nband: build\nthousands: 0\n"}
{"n":70,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0302.01","body":"## module\ntype: rule\naxioms: 8.6\n\nThis build page is the read command. It prints one face and can append to a book that already exists.\n"}
{"n":71,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0302.02","body":"## files\ntype: schema\naxioms: 8.6\n\ncore/src/bin/seqbook.rs prints one face from a book file.\n\ncore/src/book.rs Writer::open loads a book and appends. It refuses a file whose last line is torn.\n"}
{"n":72,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0302.04","body":"## module\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / module]\naxioms: 8.6.4\nwhy: The book keeps what the module is for. The repo keeps the code.\n\nThis build page is the read command. It prints one face and can append to a book that already exists.\n\n## files\ntype: why\nsource: [02 / files]\naxioms: 8.4\nwhy: The read command is the piece a person runs. The open path is how the book grows without a second writer.\n\nChecked against revision bcaaee8. The paths are the files this page names. A missing path would be a gap, not a renamed guess.\n"}
{"n":73,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0302.08","body":"## module\ntype: link\naxioms: 8.6.7\nkind: 7\nwhy: The build page points at the dev page and at the repo paths.\n\nDev page: 0402.read.\nRevision: bcaaee8.\nPaths: core/src/check.rs, core/src/bin/seqbook.rs, core/src/book.rs.\n"}
{"n":74,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0402.06.01","body":"## ran\ntype: note\naxioms: 9.6\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0502.05.01\nwhy: The run has to sit next to the MVP, not only in the test output.\n\nThe MVP on this page was run on 2026-11-11. cargo test next_pages passed with the read, why, and page-shape checks. Pack 0502.05.01 stays draft. This note is not a review.\n"}
