{"n":76,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0303.01","body":"## module\ntype: rule\naxioms: 8.6\n\nThis build page is the why check. A 01 or 02 card without a 04 why is a hard gap.\n"}
{"n":77,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0303.02","body":"## files\ntype: schema\naxioms: 8.6\n\ncore/src/check.rs why_gaps reads faces 01, 02, and 04.\n\nA missing twin, a missing why line, or a missing body is hard. A 04 body copied from face 01 is a finding.\n"}
{"n":78,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0303.04","body":"## module\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / module]\naxioms: 8.6.4\nwhy: The book keeps what the module is for. The repo keeps the code.\n\nThis build page is the why check. A 01 or 02 card without a 04 why is a hard gap.\n\n## files\ntype: why\nsource: [02 / files]\naxioms: 8.4\nwhy: The check has to name the card and the page, or a person cannot find the gap in the file.\n\nChecked against revision bcaaee8. The paths are the files this page names. A missing path would be a gap, not a renamed guess.\n"}
{"n":79,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0303.08","body":"## module\ntype: link\naxioms: 8.6.7\nkind: 7\nwhy: The build page points at the dev page and at the repo paths.\n\nDev page: 0403.why-check.\nRevision: bcaaee8.\nPaths: core/src/check.rs, core/src/bin/seqbook.rs, core/src/book.rs.\n"}
{"n":80,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0403.06.01","body":"## ran\ntype: note\naxioms: 9.6\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0503.05.01\nwhy: The run has to sit next to the MVP, not only in the test output.\n\nThe MVP on this page was run on 2026-11-11. cargo test next_pages passed with the read, why, and page-shape checks. Pack 0503.05.01 stays draft. This note is not a review.\n"}
