{"n":82,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0304.01","body":"## module\ntype: rule\naxioms: 8.6\n\nThis build page is the page-shape check. Face 00 and a content face are both required once a page has any face.\n"}
{"n":83,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0304.02","body":"## files\ntype: schema\naxioms: 8.6\n\ncore/src/check.rs page_gaps groups stored faces by page.\n\nFace 07 does not count as content. Faces 01-06 and 08 do. Draft faces count.\n"}
{"n":84,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0304.04","body":"## module\ntype: why\nsource: [01 / module]\naxioms: 8.6.4\nwhy: The book keeps what the module is for. The repo keeps the code.\n\nThis build page is the page-shape check. Face 00 and a content face are both required once a page has any face.\n\n## files\ntype: why\nsource: [02 / files]\naxioms: 8.4\nwhy: The shape check is separate from the why check so a missing stamp is not reported as a missing why.\n\nChecked against revision bcaaee8. The paths are the files this page names. A missing path would be a gap, not a renamed guess.\n"}
{"n":85,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0304.08","body":"## module\ntype: link\naxioms: 8.6.7\nkind: 7\nwhy: The build page points at the dev page and at the repo paths.\n\nDev page: 0404.page-shape.\nRevision: bcaaee8.\nPaths: core/src/check.rs, core/src/bin/seqbook.rs, core/src/book.rs.\n"}
{"n":86,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0404.06.01","body":"## ran\ntype: note\naxioms: 9.6\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0504.05.01\nwhy: The run has to sit next to the MVP, not only in the test output.\n\nThe MVP on this page was run on 2026-11-11. cargo test next_pages passed with the read, why, and page-shape checks. Pack 0504.05.01 stays draft. This note is not a review.\n"}
{"n":87,"at":"2026-11-11T19:41:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0302.06.01","body":"## copied\ntype: note\naxioms: 4.9\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0302.04, 10.10.10.0303.04, 10.10.10.0304.04\nwhy: A finding that stays in the chat is not on the page that has it.\n\nseqbook check reports a finding on 0302, 0303, and 0304. The face 04 card module repeats the face 01 body. That is the C3.2 finding, not a hard gap. The faces cannot be rewritten from here. A later draft is how the wording gets replaced.\n"}
{"n":88,"at":"2026-11-11T19:55:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0501.06.01","body":"## ran\ntype: note\naxioms: 5.6.9\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0501.05.01\nclaim: 1bf41aaf-03d9-4f17-b080-b551fe3e6781\nwhy: The pack was draft, and the page now has an AGENTS.md, so the run has a place to be recorded.\n\nBuilder read cursor/pages/10.10.10.0501/AGENTS.md and ran the pack.\n\n## w01\nresult: done\ncommand: cargo test --test first_build -- full_address bad_width leading_dot\nevidence: test result: ok. 3 passed; 0 failed.\n\n## w02\nresult: done\ncommand: cargo test --test first_build put_creates_tail_moves_from_current_and_torn_line_drops\nevidence: test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed.\n\n## w03\nresult: done\nevidence: Append is only Writer::create, Writer::open, Writer::put, and Writer::tail.\n\n## w04\nresult: done\nevidence: core/fixtures/10.11.21.book has title: timer on page 1001.\n\n## w05\nresult: done\nevidence: why: The first fixture has to show a why in the file itself, so a person can check the record without a reader program.\n\n## notes\nThe w01 ask needed the test names after --. Why: cargo accepts one filter before that mark.\n\n## unprompted\nThe builder also read core/src/bin/seqbook.rs. Why: the binary is under core/ and the append check names the writer.\n\n## overflow\nnone. Why: the five asks finished and no file was edited.\n\nLint finding: the work cards have no ask line. The page AGENTS.md held the ask. The person ordered this drafted pack to run, so the tail moved. The pack body was not rewritten. This note is the return. It is not a review, and the tail stops at return.\n"}
