{"n":92,"at":"2026-11-11T19:55:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0502.06.01","body":"## ran\ntype: note\naxioms: 5.6.9\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0502.05.01\nclaim: 0b18358d-8d4b-428f-a032-cc53f51956f1\nwhy: The pack was draft, and the page now has an AGENTS.md, so the run has a place to be recorded.\n\nBuilder read cursor/pages/10.10.10.0502/AGENTS.md and ran the pack.\n\n## w01\nresult: done\ncommand: cargo test --test next_pages open_appends_to_an_existing_book\nevidence: test open_appends_to_an_existing_book ... ok\n\n## w02\nresult: done\ncommand: cargo run --quiet -- read fixtures/10.11.21.book 10.11.21.1001.04\nevidence: why: The first fixture has to show a why in the file itself, so a person can check the record without a reader program.\nmissing: missing 10.11.21.1001.09\n\n## notes\nNo file was edited. Why: both commands passed on the code already in the grant.\n\n## unprompted\nThe test filter could have been exact. Why: it is a substring, and this run still selected the one named test.\n\n## overflow\nThe work cards have no ask line. Why: the page AGENTS.md already records that finding, and the pack body stays as written.\n\nThe person ordered this drafted pack to run, so the tail moved. This note is the return. It is not a review, and the tail stops at return.\n"}
