{"n":142,"at":"2026-11-11T21:05:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"tail","addr":"10.10.10.0502.05.02","from":"open","to":"return"}
{"n":143,"at":"2026-11-11T20:55:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0405.06.05","body":"## seq-view\ntype: note\naxioms: 5.6\nby: cursor\nrefs: SEQ-GUIDE.md\nwhy: The file type has to be decided before a pass builds it, or the pass will invent a second book.\n\nSEQ-GUIDE.md is the reader's guide. The book stays the real copy. A .seq file is a view of one page. Export makes it. A check compares booked blocks to the book. Import, when it exists, is a request and does not write.\n\nThe guide points at docs/spec/seqpage.md, face00.md, and crates/seqpage. Those files are not in this repo. This pass follows the guide. It does not claim the missing spec.\n\nMVP: export one page to text that starts with `seqpage 1`, puts face 00 first, quotes each write with its entry number, and ends with `~ end`. Check refuses a booked block that differs from the book. The book file is unchanged.\n\nNot this pass: an import queue, `.draft` addresses, the face 00 registry card, and treating this export as proof against the missing spec.\n"}
{"n":144,"at":"2026-11-11T21:00:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0405.06.06","body":"## seq-view-check\ntype: note\naxioms: 9.6\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0405.06.05\nwhy: A pass that is not checked against its own goal is only a claim.\n\nCheck: cargo test -p seqpage, 4 passed. Export of 10.10.10.0405 starts with seqpage 1, puts face 00 first, and says title := usable. The tool wrote the file and seqpage check returned ok. The book hash was unchanged. A booked line that was edited was refused. A file name whose title was cats, against a stamp of timer, was reported and not rewritten.\n\nA copy saved with a carriage return was refused. The guide allows a plain newline only. The tool's --out writes that newline.\n\nCloser: yes, to a page file a person can read and check against the book.\nNot closer: there is no import queue, the spec files named by the guide are still absent, and this export is not a draft address or a face 00 registry card.\n"}
{"n":145,"at":"2026-11-11T21:00:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0405.06.07","body":"## seq-show\ntype: note\naxioms: 5.4\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0405.06.06\nwhy: The export is only a file type a person can use if the page can show it.\n\nMVP for the next pass: open a page in the app and read its .seq view in the large pane. The compute makes the view. It does not write the book. A face in the menu still opens that face.\n"}
{"n":146,"at":"2026-11-11T21:12:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0405.06.08","body":"## seq-show-check\ntype: note\naxioms: 9.5\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0405.06.07\nwhy: The view has to be seen on the page, not only printed by a command.\n\nCheck: the app at 127.0.0.1:3210, dev band, page 0405. The large pane showed seqpage 1, face 00 first, and title := usable. Title:(usable) stayed above the address. Face .04 still opened the why. The compute served the view and did not write the book. cargo test -p compute a_seq_view_is_served_and_the_book_is_not_written passed.\n\nCloser: yes, to reading the page file in the app.\nNot closer: the pane is a view made at read time. It is not yet a file the person edits and sends back.\n"}
{"n":147,"at":"2026-11-11T21:12:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0405.06.09","body":"## seq-import\ntype: note\naxioms: 6.1\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0405.06.08, SEQ-GUIDE.md\nwhy: Export without a way back in is only a printout.\n\nMVP: a new block becomes a request. The request does not write the book. The compute then accepts or refuses that one request. A new block placed in front of the past is refused. A request that would stand a new page in one face is refused, and the file stays unchanged.\n"}
{"n":148,"at":"2026-11-11T21:12:00Z","by":"cursor","op":"put","addr":"10.10.10.0405.06.10","body":"## seq-import-check\ntype: note\naxioms: 9.6\nby: cursor\nrefs: 10.10.10.0405.06.09\nwhy: The request is only real if the book stays still until the compute decides.\n\nCheck: cargo test -p seqpage, 5 passed. A file with no new block proposes nothing. A new note after the history mark became one request and the book bytes stayed the same until propose_put. A new block placed before the booked blocks was flagged. cargo test -p compute --test import_book passed: a one-face new page was refused and the file was unchanged, then a note on the existing page was accepted and the line was in the file.\n\nCloser: yes, to sending a page view back as a request the compute can decide.\nNot closer: one request is one face. A new page still cannot be born in one request, because the stamp and its first content face are two writes. The guide's all-or-nothing proposal is not built, and the spec files are still absent, so that batch is not the next invention.\n\nNext pass waits on the spec, or on a person saying a new page may be proposed as several faces that book together or not at all.\n"}
